### Problem Description

Different platforms have different window titlebar controls order, sometimes this order even changes depending on different system settings:
1. Windows moves window controls to the left side when RTL layout is enabled (arabic languages):
<img width="493" height="331" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/222a60d0-23a8-4aba-876c-d5d13974ba7a" />

2. macOS always have constant traffic lights placement.
3. Linux allows to change order/visibility of every button in window controls depending on system settings.
<img width="656" height="65" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0baa4be0-c3fd-4bf4-a543-8e684f9e565e" />

### Proposed Solution

Implement a new Electron API:

```
declare namespace Electron {
  type NativeWindowControlType = 'close' | 'minimize' | 'maximize' | 'icon';

  interface NativeWindowControls extends NodeJS.EventEmitter {

    /**
     * Emitted when the native titlebar button order changes.
     */
    on(event: 'updated', listener: () => void): this;
    off(event: 'updated', listener: () => void): this;
    once(event: 'updated', listener: () => void): this;
    addListener(event: 'updated', listener: () => void): this;
    removeListener(event: 'updated', listener: () => void): this;

    /**
     * Returns the current native window control order on left side.
     */
    getLeadingOrder(): NativeWindowControlType[];

    /**
     * Returns the current native window control order on right side.
     */
    getTrailingOrder(): NativeWindowControlType[];
  }

  namespace Main {
    const nativeWindowControls: NativeWindowControls;
    type NativeWindowControls = Electron.NativeWindowControls;
  }
}
```

### Alternatives Considered

Hardcoding or writing such logic in every app. For linux this includes implementing watchers for GTK settings.

### Additional Information

There is an open question around "icon" control type. It can be added to API so we don't break API at some moment, but we can't reliably implement it for Linux yet, since Chromium's API provides information only for close/minimize/maximize buttons.

For windows case we can use [base::i18n::IsRTL()](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/base/%2B/master/i18n/rtl.h#54) from chromium code. Although, there seems to be no reliable way to implement watcher for this. This does not seem to be problem because Windows requires relogin to change RTL.

For Linux, electron provides [WindowButtonOrderProvider](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main/ui/views/window/window_button_order_provider.h) and [WindowButtonOrderObserver](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main/ui/linux/window_button_order_observer.h) that can provide snapshot value and attach subscriber.
